The [[Vermilion Gym]] specializes in {{type|Electric}} Pokémon. Electric-type moves are super effective against {{t|Flying}}- and {{type|Water}} Pokémon, while Electric-type Pokémon are weak to {{type|Ground}} moves.

The Gym Leader can be found in the back room, beyond a set of electric fences. Reaching him requires challengers to {{DL|Vermilion Gym|Generations III and IV|flip two switches}} hidden randomly among the many trash cans. Once the first switch has been found, the second will be in an adjacent can. If the wrong can is inspected and there is no switch inside, the puzzle resets.

[[Lt. Surge]] leads with his {{p|Raichu}}. {{m|Double Team}} makes it difficult to hit, while {{m|Thunder Wave}} {{status|Paralysis|paralyzes}} the target and cuts its {{stat|Speed}}. Surge's first {{p|Electrode}} is more defensive than the other, with Double Team and {{m|Light Screen}} letting it take less damage than normal when it does get hit. His second Electrode is more offense-oriented; {{m|Screech}} cuts the target's {{stat|Defense}}, allowing it to deal more damage with {{m|Self-Destruct|Selfdestruct}}. His final two Pokémon help to cover his team's weaknesses. Many {{type|Ground}} Pokémon are also part-{{t|Rock}}, and take serious damage from {{type|Steel}} moves like {{p|Magneton}}'s {{m|Mirror Shot}}, and {{type|Fighting}} moves like {{p|Electabuzz}}'s {{m|Low Kick}}. Electric Pokémon tend to have higher {{stat|Speed}}, so consider making use of items like [[Quick Claw]] and [[X Speed]].

